diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..31e1493 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -159,3 +159,38 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Event delivery
+
+Active webhooks receive an HTTP `POST` for subscribed events on their board. The
+JSON body contains the event's `id`, `action`, `created_at`, `board`, `creator`,
+and `eventable` (the card or comment). Slack, Campfire, and Basecamp chat URLs
+receive their native message formats instead.
+
+Requests include:
+
+- `Content-Type: application/json`
+- `X-Webhook-Delivery`: a unique delivery ID, usable as a receiver deduplication key
+- `X-Webhook-Timestamp`: the request timestamp in ISO 8601 format
+- `X-Webhook-Signature`: a hexadecimal HMAC-SHA256 of the exact request body,
+  using the webhook's signing secret
+
+Each event/webhook pair has one delivery record, and each delivery is claimed
+atomically before sending. Repeated or concurrent jobs do not send it again.
+HTTP errors and timeouts are **not retried**, and redirects are not followed.
+Requests are restricted to public IP addresses, with 10-second connection,
+read, and write timeouts.
+
+This guarantees at most one outgoing attempt, not exactly-once processing by an
+external receiver: HTTP cannot distinguish a lost response from a request that
+was never received. A worker interrupted after claiming a delivery leaves it
+`in_progress` with an unknown outcome rather than risking a duplicate POST.
+Receivers should persist the delivery ID alongside their processing result.
+
+A `2xx` response counts as success. Other HTTP responses and network errors
+count as failures and appear in the delivery log. A receiver is deactivated
+once it has at least ten consecutive failures and the failure streak spans at
+least one hour. A success or manual reactivation resets the streak. Pending
+deliveries are not sent to a deactivated receiver.
+
+Delivery logs are retained for seven days and cleaned up every 15 minutes.
